Here's how to set up runtime theme switching in .NET MAUI:

## 1. Define Theme Resource Dictionaries

Create a resource dictionary for each theme:

**Resources/Styles/LightTheme.xaml**
```xml
<ResourceDictionary xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/dotnet/2021/maui"
                    xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2009/xaml"
                    x:Class="YourApp.Resources.Styles.LightTheme">
    <Color x:Key="PageBackground">#FFFFFF</Color>
    <Color x:Key="TextPrimary">#1A1A1A</Color>
    <Color x:Key="AccentColor">#0078D4</Color>
</ResourceDictionary>
```

**Resources/Styles/DarkTheme.xaml** and **HighContrastTheme.xaml** follow the same structure with different values.

## 2. Create a Theme Service

```csharp
public enum AppTheme { Light, Dark, HighContrast }

public class ThemeService
{
    public void ApplyTheme(AppTheme theme)
    {
        var mergedDictionaries = Application.Current.Resources.MergedDictionaries;

        // Remove existing theme dictionary (keep other dictionaries intact)
        var existing = mergedDictionaries
            .FirstOrDefault(d => d is LightTheme or DarkTheme or HighContrastTheme);
        if (existing != null)
            mergedDictionaries.Remove(existing);

        // Add the selected theme
        ResourceDictionary newTheme = theme switch
        {
            AppTheme.Dark => new DarkTheme(),
            AppTheme.HighContrast => new HighContrastTheme(),
            _ => new LightTheme()
        };
        mergedDictionaries.Add(newTheme);

        // Persist the choice
        Preferences.Set("AppTheme", theme.ToString());
    }

    public AppTheme GetSavedTheme()
    {
        var saved = Preferences.Get("AppTheme", nameof(AppTheme.Light));
        return Enum.Parse<AppTheme>(saved);
    }
}
```

## 3. Apply on Startup

In **App.xaml.cs**:
```csharp
public App(ThemeService themeService)
{
    InitializeComponent();
    themeService.ApplyTheme(themeService.GetSavedTheme());
}
```

## 4. Settings Page

```csharp
public partial class SettingsPage : ContentPage
{
    private readonly ThemeService _themeService;

    public SettingsPage(ThemeService themeService)
    {
        _themeService = themeService;
        InitializeComponent();
    }

    void OnThemeSelected(object sender, EventArgs e)
    {
        var picker = (Picker)sender;
        var selected = (AppTheme)picker.SelectedIndex;
        _themeService.ApplyTheme(selected); // applies immediately
    }
}
```

## 5. Reference Theme Colors with DynamicResource

This is the key — use `DynamicResource` (not `StaticResource`) so values update at runtime:

```xml
<Label Text="Hello" TextColor="{DynamicResource TextPrimary}" />
<ContentPage BackgroundColor="{DynamicResource PageBackground}" />
```

## Key Points

- **`DynamicResource`** enables live switching without restarting.
- Keep all three dictionaries using the **same keys** so swapping is seamless.
- Use `Preferences` to persist the user's choice across launches.
- Register `ThemeService` as a singleton in `MauiProgram.cs` via `builder.Services.AddSingleton<ThemeService>()`.
